{"parentUuid":"5b806716-cb23-4bab-b076-ceaa6a688d88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011bRhxMjnuhHdRdYdKNbBNf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Second pass after `6fd6d491 polish attach guards`.\n\n## Polish commit addresses my first-pass items\n\nAll five actionable nits were fixed:\n- Tripwire comment now spells out the \"stale-summary / tree-corruption\" shape.\n- Error message dropped the misleading \"remote fetch didn't bring it in\" phrasing in favour of \"after a refresh attempt.\"\n- `runGitInDir` moved to the bottom of the test file alongside other helpers (still has `t.Helper()`).\n- Dead `--no-edit` dropped from the amend in the test.\n- Redundant `defer logging.Close()` removed from the tripwire test.\n\nLint clean; `TestAttach_*` and the full `checkpoint` package both pass locally.\n\n## Deeper pass — remaining observations\n\nNothing blocking. Three minor things worth noting:\n\n1. **Error hint hard-codes `origin`** (attach.go:290). If a user has `checkpoint_remote` configured (`getMetadataTree` tries it *before* origin), the suggested `git fetch origin entire/checkpoints/v1:entire/checkpoints/v1` may not be the right command — they'd need to fetch from their configured checkpoint remote. The fallback chain knows about this distinction but the user-facing hint doesn't. Consider detecting `remote.Configured(ctx)` and tailoring the hint, or using a more neutral \"run `entire resume` (or fetch the metadata branch from your configured remote)\". Non-blocking.\n\n2. **Refresh runs unconditionally per attach-to-trailered-commit.** Every attach to a commit with an existing `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailer now does up to 4 fetches (checkpoint_remote → treeless → full → remote-tracking). In practice the first or second succeeds cheaply, but it's worth noting this is the new cost baseline for repeat-attach workflows (research-session attaches on shared commits in CI). Fine as-is.\n\n3. **Duplicate-trailer corner case.** `resolveCheckpointID` picks `existing[len(existing)-1]` when a commit has multiple `Entire-Checkpoint:` trailers; the guard only verifies that last one. Pre-existing semantics, not introduced by this PR — just surfacing that the guard inherits it.\n\n## What I like\n\n- The split between *refuse* (attach.go) and *detect* (committed.go tripwire) is well-chosen: the refusal stops the known harmful flow, the tripwire gives a log signal if the corruption appears via a path we haven't anticipated.\n- The refresh reuses `getMetadataTree` from resume rather than re-implementing — keeps fetch fallback semantics consistent across commands.\n- `TestAttach_AppendsAsAdditionalSessionWhenIDDiffers` exercises the positive path by reading session 0 and session 1 content; that's a better guard than asserting on internal indexing.\n- Empty-checkpoint-ID degenerate case still terminates cleanly via the existing `WriteCommitted` validation.\n\nShip it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_read_input_tokens":110727,"output_tokens":1715,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1715,"cache_read_input_tokens":110727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaM6CJ9ceSBG9dmWTxYSH","type":"assistant","uuid":"92d1d2b6-8fbe-411e-872f-c1314488c9fd","timestamp":"2026-04-23T17:23:38.628Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"7d54d920-89ba-4a32-ab39-9451e7bae30c","version":"2.1.118","gitBranch":"soph/attach-checkpoint-safety"}
